<title>JAPAN: Japan Feb copper imports up 4.0 pct yr/yr--MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan Feb copper imports up 4.0 pct yr/yr--MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's refined copper imports in February rose to 23,756 tonnes, up 4.0 percent from 22,840 tonnes in the same month a year earlier, according to Finance Ministry data released on Friday.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		    Feb 97	  Jan 97	 Feb 96</p>
<p> Total	    23,756	  27,526	 22,840</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Chile	    12,869	   9,378	  9,356</p>
<p> U.S.		2,523	   3,536	  5,481</p>
<p> Zambia	    1,052	   5,860	  1,294</p>
<p>Imports in the first two months of calendar 1997 were 51,282 tonnes, up 11.3 percent from 46,057 tonnes during the same period last year.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
